ival_rate":0.9706,"ask_survival_n":34}},"skipped_slates":[],"book_gap":{"status":"not_run","label":"Book vs Kalshi (model-free) \u2014 PAPER ONLY","reason":"The archive curve needs the Oct 18\u2013Nov 11 alt-price archive, which is not in this repository; nothing is fitted or logged until it is supplied.","rows":[]},"his_record":null,"his_record_placeholder":"Grading in progress \u2014 20 posted ladders transcribed.","method":["The tool searches every Kalshi single-leg rung (points, rebounds, assists, threes) for the biggest gap between our model's probability and the price, after Kalshi's fee.","It is Sam's method \u2014 a tool-driven search of alt rungs at fixed targets \u2014 rebuilt on Kalshi singles; sportsbook prices are reference only, never a venue.","Model probabilities are the ladder's live published numbers for every stat; the points recalibration map is in shadow and prices nothing until it ships.","Legs are ranked by per-leg z (edge over the break-even's standard deviation) in four fixed runs a day, one per stat, top three player-game clusters each, no re-runs.","Everything here is paper. Staking is a separate CEO decision after the locked gate."],"guard":{"version":"sam_v1+guard_v1","rule":"backtests/sam_method_guard_rule.md","edge_cap_points":10.0,"minutes_move":3.0,"text":"Outlier guard (registered before the first counted run): a leg is dropped when its claimed edge is above 10 points or the player's projected minutes moved more than 3 from the morning build. The largest gaps are usually the model's own projection errors."},"readings":["P shown is the probability of the listed side.","A strike that is not a ladder rung is not priced.","Off-schedule (manual) runs are shown but count toward no gate."]}